  There are also ways to speed up the '/' command.
  - Use ',' on the object/monster.  
    - That way you don't get the annoying "More info" prompt.
  - Cursor navigation shortcuts:
    - Lowercase navigation letters move one space at a time.
    - Uppercase navigation letters move TEN spaces at a time.
    - Press special terrain letters to move to that terrain, e.g.:
      - '<' moves the cursor directly to the upstairs
      - '>' moves the cursor directly to the downstairs
      - '_' moves the cursor directly to an altar.  
        - Repeat '_' to cycle through all the altars on a level.
      - '^' moves the cursor directly to a trap.
        - Repeat '^' to cycle through all the altars on a level.
      - That means it's easy to get the cursor to a unique terrain
        type near a monsters.

  Note that the move command, '_' and the teleport control use the same
movement keys/shortcuts as above.

  If part of your problem is not knowing the item letters, here's a
quick reference:

  [ is armor
  ) is a weapon
  ( is a tool
  % is food
  / is a wand
  ! is a potion

  These are important to learn because they are also used as shortcut
keys in the interface.  E.g. 

  - Press ')' and you'll be shown the weapons you're wielding.
    - Great when digging with pickaxe
    - To double-check that you're twoweaponing.
  - Press '[' to see what armor you're wearing. 
    - (Great for post-foocubus dalliance.)
  - Press '*' to see everything you're currently using, 
    - including all of the above and 
      - quivered weapons (should be in the weapon display.  Bug report?)
    - lit lamps, candles, etc.

