  But wait, there's more!

  In the 'I' inventory command you can just press the symbol for the
inventory type: ')' selects the weapons you're carrying to be shown.

  The 'd'rop, ',' (pickup), #loot, and 'a'pplying a container are
commands where these really get useful.

  Just like you can drop all items of unknown inventory status using
'X', you can select item types with the item symbol characters.  If I
want to drop all spellbooks it's just "D+ , "  Inventory letters don't
matter, so there's no thought involved.

  To get all spellbooks from my BoH:
   'abo+ , '  
  and put them into a container:
   '#lo<RET>y i+ , '
   Then hold down the spacebar until all the spellbooks are in.  

  Completely automatic finger macros.  People who've watched my games
comment on my playing speed.  That's not really fast play, just a fast
interface.  That's also why I always use the same inventory letters for
the same things, e.g. a credit card, lockpick, or key is always 'k'.
candle, lamp, lantern, magic lamp is always 'l'.

  When selling after credit cloning it's very helpful in a hardware or
book/scroll shop.  'D+? +?' selects all scrolls and spellbooks and drops
them.  The items selected that way don't even have to be onscreen.  They
can be pushed off by the length of the inventory and they'll still get
selected.




